    58	### Proof bottlenecks
    59	
    60	1. **Universal landing plus a cofinal generic-degree bound.** No collection of rank-four or other bounded-class exclusions proves JC2 until arbitrary Keller maps land faithfully in the charged architecture and the “always a next degree” escape is closed [A:171–172, 190–191].
    61	2. **All-degree typing of the dicritical budget.** The proof `2m <= N-1` is reviewed only in the plane degree-four canonical setting, and the integration expressly forbids exporting Orevkov names beyond that scope without rebuilding the hypotheses [R4:19–47].
    62	3. **Algebraic attainment of surviving one-place data.** Colourability is only a necessary condition, and explicit survivors at `Delta_aff=6,7,9,10,12,13,15,...` leave the actual charged-curve realization problem untouched [A:12–22; W:20–31].
    63	4. **One concrete SNC boundary model for the one-cusp horn.** All abstract identities needed for the four-row partition are promoted, but neither `d_h` nor `r_h` exists as campaign data until one charged coordinate is resolved [R4:73–90].
    64	5. **Topology beyond the clean one-node case.** The promoted meridional obstruction says nothing about tangencies, unibranch affine conductors, additional singularities, nonsimple inertia, or disconnected covers [H:91–96].
    65	
    66	### Disproof bottlenecks
    67	
    68	1. **Uniform polynomial complexity.** The AS seed lifts through every Witt level only by growing support/degree and converges to a nonpolynomial restricted-analytic object, so a counterexample needs one support bound surviving all levels [A:175, 208].
    69	2. **Formal-germ algebraization with route provenance.** Modular nonemptiness, compatible jets, a characteristic-zero formal germ, and a polynomial Keller map are four distinct stages; K00 remains stuck at the last two and can also lose its source route during gluing [A:193].
    70	3. **Global nonproperness/collision, not merely `J=1`.** A finite-support lift or sparse solution is useful only if it also carries a certified off-diagonal collision or equivalent global nonproperness datum; otherwise it can simply be an automorphism.
    71	4. **A source-complete search grammar above the classical firewalls.** Below the known bounds the region is already empty, while above them generic sparse supports overwhelmingly miss the thin Keller locus [A:225, 278].
