   110	## 3. New avenue / mechanism
   111	
   112	**Heegaard-Floer / semigroup-distribution attainment obstructions on the survivor
   113	delta-sequences** (new engine; not in any of the 46 rows or overlays, which record
   114	only splice admissibility, colouring, and log-BMY for this class).
   115	
   116	Setting, from the promoted structure: a charged survivor is a reduced irreducible
   117	plane curve `B`, one place at infinity, `A1` normalization (rational), sole affine
   118	singularity unibranch with semigroup `S_a` of conductor `2*Delta_aff` (plane-branch
   119	semigroups are symmetric, so conductor `= 2*delta`). Its projective closure is a
   120	**rational cuspidal curve with at most two cusps** — the affine cusp and possibly
   121	the place at infinity — of some degree `d`, with
   122	`delta_infty = (d-1)(d-2)/2 - Delta_aff >= 0`, and with `S_infty` constrained by the
   123	Abhyankar–Moh semigroup theorem (delta-sequence divisibility conditions) because the
   124	place at infinity is one place.
   125	
   126	Rational cuspidal plane curves are exactly the class where the strongest modern
   127	nonexistence technology lives and has never been aimed at this campaign: the FLMN
   128	semigroup distribution property (Fernández de Bobadilla–Luengo–Melle-Hernández–
   129	Némethi, Proc. LMS 2006), proved for cuspidal curves via Heegaard-Floer d-invariants
   130	(Borodzik–Livingston, JEMS 2014) and lattice cohomology (Bodnár–Némethi), with
   131	multi-cusp counting versions via semigroup infimum-convolution (Bodnár–Celoria–
   132	Golla); plus Varchenko spectrum semicontinuity and Orevkov's sharp BMY-type
   133	multiplicity inequality; plus, in the unicuspidal one-Puiseux-pair regime, a
   134	*complete classification* (the FLMN Fibonacci-type list). Exact statements and the
   135	multi-cusp counting form must be literature-pinned at execution; I flag that now
   136	rather than consume it.
