   104	## 3. New avenue or mechanism
   105	
   106	**Residual unramified sheet of the unique rank-four branch.**
   107	
   108	This is not “apply Abhyankar–Moh,” not “run more colourings,” and not “generalize `m=1` by copying `2m <= N-1`.”
   109	
   110	**Setup, from promoted facts only.** An actual rank-four proper block has irreducible reduced charged branch `B`, `normalization(B)=A1`, and generic branch partition `(2,1,1)` or `(3,1)` with one ramification point (`H_inertia` at `5d7df7ce…:84–104`, consumed by the `m=1` integration). So a generic point of `B subset A_F` has fibre cycle type either one 2-cycle plus two 1-cycles, or one 3-cycle plus one 1-cycle. Write `B^sm` for the smooth locus of `B`. The unique ramified preimage along generic `B` is the ramified sheet. The complementary preimages form an unramified covering `Sigma -> B^sm` of degree 2 in the `(2,1,1)` case and degree 1 in the `(3,1)` case. These are *sheets of the finite map*, not dicritical divisors and not flags of a compactification. Flag/place/series: this covering is not identified with an Orevkov dicritical, nor with a physical place of `B`, nor with the cover series of a splice diagram.
   111	
   112	**Mechanism.** Because `B` is rational with `A1` normalization, `B^sm` is isomorphic to `A1` minus a finite set of punctures (the preimages of the affine singularities). The residual map `Sigma -> B^sm` is unramified of degree 1 or 2; it need not be connected. Connectedness is typed `OPEN` until a lemma says otherwise.
   113	
   114	- `(3,1)`: degree 1, so a section of `F` over `B^sm`. A holomorphic section of a nonproper map along its nonproper-value curve cannot extend to a proper section over all of `B` (that would split `F` over `B` and contradict that `B` consists of nonproper values: Chau 2003, `A_F` is the union of images of dicritical series). The obstruction is therefore *extension across the affine singularities and across infinity*. If the section extends through every affine singularity, `B` would carry a polynomial right-inverse on a Zariski-open of itself; that is a coordinate-recognition statement on the unique `A_F` component, i.e. a correctly typed Abhyankar–Moh client (row 6), not the old multi-place fibre abuse. If it cannot extend, the obstruction is supported at the singularities and is therefore a function of the δ-sequence / conductor of `B`.
   115	- `(2,1,1)`: degree 2, either two sections or a connected étale double cover of `B^sm`. Two sections reduce to the `(3,1)` extension problem with multiplicity two. A connected double cover of `A1 minus s` punctures is classified by the subset of punctures of odd ramification (plus possibly infinity). The numerical semigroup of a one-place curve determines those punctures (Assi–García-Sánchez, arXiv:1407.0490: a δ-sequence determines the semigroup, the conductor, and the affine singularities). A colourable survivor whose semigroup cannot carry either two sections or such a double cover is combinatorially unrealizable as `A_F`, even though it is colourable as a braid. Which of the two topologies occurs is `OPEN` until typed; do not fill by cap.
   116	
   117	**Why this is new.** Colouring sees meridians of the *link at infinity* acting as transpositions in `S_4`. The residual sheet sees the *restriction of `F` along `B` itself*. Those representations are conjugate only after one uses C1 (meridians of the knot and of the irreducible curve are conjugate) *and* a path from a fibre meridian to a meridian of `B`; that path is exactly the conjugacy sentence the one-node packet made mandatory, and it is not automatic for cabled/unibranch conductors. The avenue therefore attacks the survivors that the one-node theorem does not reach, with a covering of `B^sm` rather than a graph-knot of the smoothing.
   118	
   119	**Primary literature.** Chau, *Two remarks on non-zero constant Jacobian polynomial maps of `C^2`*, Ann. Polon. Math. 82.1 (2003), Lemma 5: `A_F` equals the union of images of dicritical series. Orevkov 1987, (4) and Cor. 4.3, used only as already typed at plane rank four (no export). Assi–García-Sánchez, *Algorithms for curves with one place at infinity*, J. Symbolic Comput. / arXiv:1407.0490, for the semigroup-to-punctures dictionary. Galindo–Monserrat–Moreno-Ávila–Moyano-Fernández, *On δ-sequences and surfaces at infinity*, arXiv:2408.15931, for the dual graph of the resolution at infinity from a δ-sequence. Neumann–Rudolph unfolding and Neumann's minimal-Seifert theorem as already consumed by the promoted one-node packet (C1 mandatory).
   120	
   121	**What it is not.** It is not a claim that `m=1` holds at every degree. It is not an identification of the residual cover with a dicritical. If the extension obstruction cannot be typed, the output is `OPEN`, not a cap.
   122	
   123	## 4. New connection between existing avenues
   124	
   125	**Orevkov remainder on the unique branch equals the numerical excess that the one-cusp table reads as `Theta_h`.**
