   358	
   359	### Strongest proof attack: the cusp-local-group law as an attainment filter
   360	
   361	The saturation result says the colouring ladder can no longer *exclude*
   362	a conductor; the surviving rows are exactly those admitting a
   363	meridian-to-transposition colouring. Identity (M) at `nu = 0` turns
   364	colourability from a *permission* into a *quota*:
   365	
   366	> `sum_{p in Sing(A_F)} #Fix(H_p) = sigma*(s-1) + 1`, `sigma = #Fix(g)`.
   367	
   368	In the charged quartic transposition class `sigma = 2`, so the quota is
   369	`2s - 1`: **exactly one cusp may have a two-generated local image
   370	(`#Fix = 1`, forcing `H_p =~ S_3` inside a point stabiliser), and every
   371	other cusp must have cyclic local image `<g>` (`#Fix = 2`).** For a
   372	unicuspidal row (`s=1`) the quota is `1`: the single cusp's local group
   373	must have exactly one fixed point, i.e. the cusp knot must admit a
   374	meridian-to-transposition representation **onto `S_3`, not onto `Z/2`
   375	and not onto anything with a different fixed-point count**.
